      "text": "**Ancient roots**: Homer's Iliad describes a boxing contest at Patroclus's funeral games (Book 23). Greek boxing (pygme) in the Olympics from 688 BCE -- see Ancient Athletics guide. Roman caestus: glove loaded with metal (lead, iron studs, sometimes blades) -- more weapon than protection, made fights shorter and more brutal."
    },
