      "text": "LONDON PRIZE RING RULES (1838):\n  -- Updated Broughton system\n  -- Round ends when man goes down\n  -- 30 seconds to reach scratch mark\n  -- Square (7-foot sided ring) marked in grass\n  -- No headbutting, gouging, biting\n  -- Wrestling/clinching extensively permitted\n  -- Fight length: potentially hundreds of rounds\n  -- Record: Jack Jones vs Patsy Tunney, 1825: 276 rounds"
