      },
      "text": "**John L. Sullivan (1858-1918)**: Last recognized bare-knuckle heavyweight champion. Title from 1882 (defeating Paddy Ryan). Famous for \"I can lick any son of a bitch in the house\" touring challenge. Won 75 bouts. Refused to fight Black challengers -- maintained explicit color line. Last bare-knuckle championship fight: July 8, 1889, vs Jake Kilrain, 75 rounds, 2 hours 16 minutes, in Richburg, Mississippi. Sullivan won; prosecution followed (illegal fight). Subsequent career: under Queensberry Rules. Lost to \"Gentleman Jim\" Corbett, September 7, 1892 (round 21)."
    },
