      "text": "| Champion | Reign | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| John L. Sullivan | 1882-1892 | Last bare-knuckle; refused Black opponents |\n| Jack Johnson | 1908-1915 | First Black heavyweight champion; \"Great White Hope\" media frenzy |\n| Jack Dempsey | 1919-1926 | \"Manassa Mauler\"; crowd attendance records |\n| Joe Louis | 1937-1949 | 25 title defenses; 12 years champion; symbolic anti-fascism vs Schmeling |\n| Rocky Marciano | 1952-1956 | 49-0 career, 43 KO; only heavyweight to retire undefeated |\n| Sonny Liston | 1962-1964 | Destroyed Floyd Patterson twice; KO'd in round 1 and 2 by Ali |\n| Muhammad Ali (Cassius Clay) | 1964-1979 (intermittent) | Greatest promoter; Vietnam refusal; rope-a-dope; cultural icon |\n| Mike Tyson | 1986-1990 (first reign) | Youngest heavyweight champion (20); devastating first-round knockout power |\n| Lennox Lewis | 1993-2004 (intermittent) | British-Canadian; unified champion multiple times |\n| Wladimir Klitschko | 2006-2015 | Ukrainian; dominant 9-year reign, \"brothers era\" |"
