      "text": "**Muhammad Ali**: Cassius Clay won heavyweight title from Liston (February 25, 1964), announced conversion to Islam, adopted name Muhammad Ali. Refused Vietnam draft induction April 28, 1967: \"I ain't got no quarrel with them Viet Cong.\" Stripped of title, boxing license revoked, sentenced to 5 years (conviction overturned by Supreme Court 1971). Exile 1967-1970 -- peak athletic years lost. Returned, \"Rumble in the Jungle\" (Kinshasa 1974 vs George Foreman): rope-a-dope strategy (Ali absorbed punishment against ropes, let Foreman exhaust himself, then knocked him out round 8). Career record: 56-5, 37 KO."
